(defcustom palette-common-user nil
  "Common user-defined colors to extend all the themes' palettes.
This is meant to extend the palette of the active theme with
custom named colors and/or semantic palette mappings.  Those may then be
used in combination with palette overrides (see
`palette-common-overrides')."
  :group 'theme
  :type '(repeat (list symbol (choice symbol string)))
  )

(defcustom palette-common-overrides nil
  "Set palette overrides for all the themes.

Mirror the elements of a theme's palette, overriding their value.
The palette variables are named `palette-THEME-NAME', while
individual theme overrides are `palette-THEME-NAME-overrides'.
The THEME-NAME is one of the symbols in `theme-items'.  For
example:

- `palette-light'
- `palette-light-overrides'

Individual theme overrides take precedence over these common
overrides.

The idea of common overrides is to change semantic color
mappings, such as to make the cursor red.  Whereas theme-specific
overrides can also be used to change the value of a named color,
such as what hexadecimal RGB value the red-warmer symbol
represents."
  :group 'theme
  :version "30.1"
  :type '(repeat (list symbol (choice symbol string)))
  )



